O Standard Generalized Markup Language (SGML) é uma {{Glossary(“ISO”)}} especificação que veio para definir as declarações/sintaxe Linguagens de Marcação. 
On the web, {{Glossary(“HTML”)}} 4, {{Glossary(“XHTML”)}}, and {{Glossary(“XML”)}} are popular SGML-based languages. 
It is worth noting that since its fifth edition, HTML is no longer SGML-based and has its own parsing rules. 
