Which loop type should you use? 
For basic uses, for, while, and do...while loops are largely interchangeable. 
They can all be used to solve the same problems, and which one you use will largely depend on your personal preference — which one you find easiest to remember or most intuitive. 
Let’s have a look at them again. 
First for: 
for (initializer; exit-condition; final-expression) { 
// code to run 
} 
while: 
initializer 
while (exit-condition) { 
// code to run 
final-expression 
} 
and finally do...while: 
initializer 
do { 
// code to run 
final-expression 
} while (exit-condition) 
Nota: There are other loop types/features too, which are useful in advanced/specialized situations and beyond the scope of this article. 
If you want to go further with your loop learning, read our advanced Loops and iteration guide. 
Conclusion 
This article has revealed to you the basic concepts behind, and different options available when, looping code in JavaScript. 
You should now be clear on why loops are a good mechanism for dealing with repetitive code, and be raring to use them in your own examples! 
If there is anything you didn’t understand, feel free to read through the article again, or contact us to ask for help. 
